        "The perf levers THIS substrate scope OWNS — the foundation the upgraded variants tune on top of: SG_TUNED_TILE_N=128, SG_TUNED_TILE_M=128 (wgmma.cuh:133-138); SG_TUNED_PIPE_DEPTH=2, SG_TUNED_WG_COUNT=2, SG_TUNED_PROD_REGS=40, SG_TUNED_CONS_REGS=232 (tile_pipeline.cuh:86-97); SG_TUNED_MEGA_BLOCK=256 (megakernel_common.cuh:50); SG_TUNED_PSCAN_BLOCK=512 (types.h:42). All #ifndef-guarded so the autotuner injects -DSG_TUNED_* per-TU; the baked-upgraded variants are pre-tuned values of exactly these knobs. The DEC_FWD_PIPE +1.49x deeper-ring lever tunes PIPE_DEPTH.",
        "No prebuilt binaries are in the assigned read scope (all 10 are source headers + one .cu). Prebuilt cubins/objects live under build/, .build_cache/, nvcc_baseline_build/, task11_bench_build/, _dectc_codegen/ (seen in root listing) — flagged for the artifact reader, not read here.",
        "mma.cuh CUTLASS GEMM flavors are all 128x128x64 tile / 1x1x1 cluster / FP32 accumulate / KernelScheduleAuto: Sm90Gemm, Sm90GemmBT (LayoutBT templated B/Bt), Sm90GemmBTOut (typed output, no fp32 scratch+cast), Sm90GemmAT (ColumnMajor-A At for ViT wgrad). Two DOCUMENT-STOPs reject small-M and Cooperative-large-M variants (double nvcc cost near OOM, unmeasured no-GPU win). TF32 path reinterprets float as tfloat32_t; explicitly NOT bit-identical to scalar FP32. Operator cache (16-slot thread_local, keyed {M,N,K,A,B,C}) reuses baked TMA descriptors on hit."
