      "corrections": [
        "The hand-rolled megakernel staging path uses cp.async, NOT TMA — any prior-pass claim that the L3 megakernel hand-writes TMA staging is wrong for these files: TMA exists ONLY inside CUTLASS's auto-generated CollectiveBuilder mainloop. mma.cuh:145-153 itself notes there is no hand-written TMA staging in mma.cuh to inject elect/mbarrier into.",
        "DEVIATION: the wgmma.cuh API doc (wgmma.cuh:418-421) says the canonical operand orientation is TransA=0,TransB=1, but the actually-gated/exercised path (tile_pipeline.cuh:335-339 and wgmma_selftest.cu:110-111) uses TransA=0,TransB=0 ('both Major-K, cute Major::K==0'). The TransB=0 form is what is validated against torch.",
        "wgmma_selftest.cu must NOT be counted as part of the shipped setup.py build — it is JIT-loaded test-only and is explicitly filtered out of the _ops glob (PyInit__ops collision), per setup.py:455-468.",
        "The 'CUTLASS WGMMA path' (mma.cuh) and the 'in-kernel ss-wgmma path' (wgmma.cuh) are two distinct mechanisms; CUTLASS is rejected for the L3 persistent megakernel (device-non-callable). Conflating them would mis-attribute TMA to the megakernel."
